From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:15:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the performance overlay of
 Playtendoh's Switch side

The overlay is the one Eden's program draws for Playtendoh's Switch side (ProsperoEdenX's hud.h,
vulkan_hud.frag and their checks): a chip against the corner the settings name, its line in
Montserrat from the same baked table as the loading screen's words, in its inks, and the same
pieces: "VLK 960x540 27FPS 37.0MS CPU 55% 40% 12% 8% GPU 43% MEM 4.1/16.0G GFX 2.5G", where this
program's line was a 3x5 pixel font saying "VLK F27 S100 W37 C55 G43 M4.2G".

- hud.h: Eden's line, chip and fields (every piece by default, the CPU core by core, the game's own
  resolution), the snapshot marked by a bit the loading screen never sets.
- loading_text.glsl and hud_text_advances.h from ProsperoEdenX's bake-loading-text.py (its glyph
  fields as they are there, so the line looks the same); the loading screen's helpers now come from
  that file, its name line says LICHII and its colours are Playtendoh's Switch red.
- performance.cpp: each of the four emulated cores' load, the memory pool's size and what is taken
  of it, and what the Vulkan allocator holds (prepare-vulkan-port.py), as Eden's program reads them.
- The game's resolution taken as each frame reaches the display (vulkan_guest_resolution.inc).
- The OpenGL path draws the same chip; fps_overlay_colors is kept with the other overlay settings.
